<title>CANADA: CNR to cut 133 revenue management jobs.</title>
<headline>CNR to cut 133 revenue management jobs.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian National Railway Co said on Thursday that it planned to cut 133 jobs as part of the consolidation of its four revenue management centers.</p>
<p>The centers, located in Edmonton, Toronto, Detroit and Montreal, would be consolidated to Toronto, resulting in savings of C$40 million over five years.</p>
<p>A total of 40 permanent positions and 93 temporary positions would therefore be eliminated, the company said.</p>
<p>((Reuters Montreal bureau 514-985-2434))</p>
